-- title:
--   Gradient bound for the comparison difference, with constants independent of $\delta$
-- statement:
--   Notation. $S=[-3,3]^2$ is the model square; a metric is a smooth positive matrix field $g$; $z$ is a scalar height; $H=\nabla_g^2z$ is its covariant Hessian; $K_g$ is the Gaussian curvature; $E=\det g\,(1-|dz|_g^2)$; $q=H_{xy}/H_{yy}$ is the Hessian quotient; $\kappa(x^2-h(y))$ is the model curvature; the patch box and the central box are the squares $[-1/10,1/10]^2$ and $[-1/5,1/5]^2$; the sheared coordinates are $\xi=x,\ \theta=y+q_0x$, with sheared height $z_s$; $L$ and $v_*$ are the class width and speed of (4.2); $\tilde g_\tau$ is the test metric (4.12) built from $g_*$; a bounded admissible height of bound $M$ is an admissible height with (4.1).
--
--   Let $g_*$ be smooth and positive on an open $V\supseteq S$ with $C^2$ bound $G$ and $\det g_*\ge d$ on $S$, and fix $\kappa,q_0,M$. There is $r\in(0,1/2)$ with $Lr\le1/20$ and $r$ small such that for every $N>2$ there are $C_{\mathrm{res}},C_{\mathrm{source}},C_{\mathrm{gradient}}$ such that for $0<\delta\le1/2$ and all large $\tau$: for every patch perturbation $\eta$, flow data and bounded admissible height $z$ of bound $M$ with the usual bounds and $g$ within $\tau^{-\tau}$ of the test metric, the Taylor approximation $P$ of the sheared height has residual of size $\le C_{\mathrm{res}}\tau^{-N}$ with weighted moment at most $2C_{\mathrm{res}}\big(\int\chi\big)\delta\,\tau^{-(N+1)}$, the source satisfies $|F|\le C_{\mathrm{source}}\tau^{2-N}$, and for $|\theta|\le\delta/\tau$, $i\in\{1,2\}$,
--
--   $$\Big(\int_{|x|\le Lr/16}\big(\partial_i(P-z_s)\big)^2(x,\theta)\,dx\Big)^{1/2}\le C_{\mathrm{gradient}}\,\delta\,\tau^{1-N}.$$
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This is the upstream Lean declaration `OAI.SmoothLocal.Perturbation.exists_actual_uniform_comparison_gradient` in `lean/OAI/Geometry/IsometricImmersion/Comparison/ActualUniformComparisonGradient.lean`, stated verbatim; the Lean statement is authoritative for the precise hypotheses. It is an intermediate result of OpenAI's formalization.
